19 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Map of India highlighting a location with geo-references 21°08'48.5"N and 79°03'01.7"E. Several images depict trees in a field, irrigation equipment, and components numbered 1 to 7. At the bottom, a layout shows an irrigation system with labels like \215Fertilization Unit,\216 \215Main Line,\216 \215Inline Lateral,\216 \215Flush Valve,\216 and \215Water Resources,\216 alongside multiple lines labeled T1-T6 and R2-R4, indicating a detailed irrigation setup.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Bar chart depicting monthly variations over a year in several metrics: ETr in blue bars, Kc in red bars, WA in green bars, SDI as a purple line, and DI as a turquoise line. Data points are labeled with specific values. Time phases are marked as SP, NLIP, CDP, CM, and CH with varying durations. Vertical axes show SDI and DI values on the left and ETr, Kc, and WA on the right.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Bar chart showing the percentage of graded fruits across six treatments \(T1 to T6\). Each treatment has three categories: A \(greater than eighty millimeters\), B \(seventy to eighty millimeters\), and C \(less than seventy millimeters\). Category B consistently has the highest percentage, followed by C, with A having the lowest.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Bar charts comparing leaf nutrient content across six treatments. Left chart shows macro-nutrients \(N, P, K, Ca, Mg\) as percentages. Right chart shows micro-nutrients \(Fe, Mn, Cu, Zn\) in parts per million. Bars display nutrient levels with labels indicating statistical significance.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Correlation matrix depicting various leaf and fruit attributes and their relationships. Circular color-coded cells range from blue to red, indicating correlation strengths, with blue representing positive and red negative correlations. Asterisks indicate statistical significance. Labels include variables like \215Yield\216, \215Leaf-N\216, and \215Fruit-Ca\216. A vertical color gradient on the right denotes the correlation scale from -1 to 1.) /K 1 /P 9 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
24 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Line graph comparing plant variable values based on eigenvalues, percentage variance, and cumulative percentage of variance. Three lines represent different parameters: green for leaf physiological parameters, red for fruit nutrients and leaf physiological parameters, and blue for leaf nutrients and leaf physiological parameters. The green line shows the highest values, followed by the red and blue lines.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
25 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Scatter plot comparing forecasted yield to observed yield, displayed in tons per hectare. Red data points show a positive correlation along a trendline, with a root mean square error of 0.9825 and an R-squared value of 0.956.) /K 1 /P 9 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
26 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Bar charts showing macro and micro nutrient contents in fruits under six treatments \(T1 to T6\). Left chart displays macro nutrients \(N, P, K, Ca, Na, Mg\) in grams per kilogram, with nitrogen \(N\) showing the highest values. Right chart presents micro nutrients \(Fe, Mn, Cu, Zn\) in grams per kilogram, with iron \(Fe\) having the highest values. Error bars and significance letters indicate variability and statistical differences between treatments.) /K 0 /P 9 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
